<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kanagawa Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kanagawa Prefecture is a prefecture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> on the south-west side of Tokyo Bay, with its capital at Yokohama. It covers the former province of Sagami and part of Musashi, including the old castle town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odawara">Odawara</a>, and was formed after the abolition of the domains in 1871. Its ports, above all Yokohama, were central to Japan's opening to foreign trade from 1859.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kanagawa-prefecture.jpg" alt="Kanagawa Prefecture" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dick Thomas Johnson from Tokyo, Japan · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yokohama_(52978652484).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
